course: dictionary
lesson: 9411
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Squat is one of them. It can be a movement, a thing you do in a gym, a shape, or even a way of living. To find the right meaning, read the words around it: they are its context.
explain: «Hopak is a lively Ukrainian folk dance with big jumps and squat-kicks, linked to Cossack traditions.» Squat-kicks are part of a dance, so squat here means bending your knees low. It cannot mean living in an empty building, because that would not fit a dance. Always try your meaning in the sentence to check it.
explain: «The hardest dances, like ballet on the tips of the toes or the big squat-kicks of hopak, need years of training for strength and balance.» Strength and balance are clues that the movement is hard and uses your legs. This is why dancers build up slowly with a teacher, just as you would for a squat in PE.
fact: Squat can be a verb (to squat), a noun (a squat), or an adjective (squat, short and wide).
fact: «To squat» means to bend your knees and lower your body so you sit on your heels or just above the ground.
fact: A squat in exercise means bending your knees and standing up again, keeping your back straight. Squats make your leg muscles strong.
fact: «Squat» as an adjective means short and wide, as in «a squat little teapot».
fact: «To squat» can also mean living in an empty building or on land without permission. In some places, like homes in England, this is a crime.
exercise: «Hopak is a lively Ukrainian folk dance with big jumps and squat-kicks, linked to Cossack traditions.» What does squat mean here? | Short and wide | Nothing at all | Living in an empty house | *Bending your knees low and kicking
exercise: «A squat little teapot sat on the table.» What does squat mean here? | Tall and thin | *Short and wide | Cold and wet | Very hot
exercise: Jayden says, «You know squat.» In US slang, what does squat mean? | Ten pounds | Something very big | *Nothing at all | A kind of dance
test: Ruby says, «I did ten squats in PE.» What does squat mean? | Jump as high as you can | *Bend your knees and stand up again | Short and fat | Live in an empty building
test: «The squat toad sat on the log.» What does squat mean here? | *Short and fat | Singing loudly | Covered in mud | Very fast
exam: Why do the dancers in «the big squat-kicks of hopak» need years of training? | To win a prize every week | *To build strength and balance safely | To learn to read music | Because the teacher is strict
